  "updatedAt": "2026-03-05T20:42:23.778Z",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nVectorized, numerically stable reference implementation following exact specifications.\n\n### 💻 Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef streaming_minmax(D: int, batches: list, eps: float = 1e-8) -> dict:\n    all_data = np.vstack(batches)\n    mn = np.min(all_data, axis=0)\n    mx = np.max(all_data, axis=0)\n    denom = np.where(mx == mn, 1.0, mx - mn)\n    normed = []\n    for b in batches:\n        b_arr = np.array(b, dtype=float)\n        normed.append(np.round((b_arr - mn) / denom, 6).tolist())\n    return {\n        'normalized_batches': normed,\n        'min': np.round(mn, 6).tolist(),\n        'max': np.round(mx, 6).tolist()\n    }\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the input dimensions.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ for memory buffers.\n",
